@startuml auto-sequence
title M3c sequential auto reservation, StopAuto and CancelRun
actor Caller
participant InspectionEngine as Engine
participant "Auto session" as Auto
participant "Same run path / Runner" as Run
participant TimeProvider as Clock
Caller -> Engine : StartAuto(job, interval, timeout, maxRuns)
Engine -> Engine : reserve AutoId and first RunId under shared lock
Engine -> Auto : start loop with first run handle
Engine --> Caller : Accepted / auto.Completion
loop until a terminal outcome is chosen
par current inspection
Engine ->> Run : Prepare -> Acquire -> Inspect -> Persist
Run --> Auto : run.Completion (including cleanup)
else optional caller requests while run is active
opt stop future runs
Caller -> Engine : StopAuto(autoId)
Engine -> Auto : prohibit next admission / leave current run intact
Engine --> Caller : Accepted
end
opt also cancel current work
Caller -> Engine : CancelRun(currentRunId)
Engine -> Run : request stop (Persisting returns TooLate)
end
end
Auto -> Auto : count completion / retain last run only
alt Succeeded, no stop, below run limit
Auto -> Clock : Task.Delay(interval, provider, schedule token)
note over Engine, Clock
Mode=Automatic, IsBusy=false while waiting.
Manual Start / another StartAuto still returns Busy with BusyAutoId.
end note
opt StopAuto while waiting
Caller -> Engine : StopAuto(autoId)
Engine -> Auto : prohibit next admission / cancel schedule delay only
Engine --> Caller : Accepted
end
Clock --> Auto : delay completed or canceled
opt delay succeeded and no stop won the admission lock
Auto -> Engine : admit next RunId under shared lock
end
else stop requested, run limit reached or run failed
Auto -> Auto : finish repetition / preserve last run diagnostics
end
end
Auto -> Auto : finish schedule cancellation delivery / dispose schedule token
Auto -> Engine : release auto reservation / save final snapshot
Engine --> Caller : auto.Completion
note over Caller, Engine
StopAuto and next admission share the engine lock.
If admission wins, StopAuto leaves that run intact.
Engine disposal stops scheduling AND requests current Shutdown,
then waits for both run and session cleanup.
end note
@enduml
